abstract: >-
  SysSimX is a Python framework for heterogeneous hybrid co-simulation
  with runtime model switching. It couples Functional Mock-up Units
  (FMUs), OpenSim models, and NGSolve-based transient structural-dynamics
  models through a shared component abstraction, derives structural execution metadata
  for initialization, master algorithm execution, and algebraic-loop
  handling, and supports hybrid event localization and runtime switching
  between alternative models of the same subsystem. Switching is declared as
  a map from a scalar signal onto ordered model regions, and each transition
  is localized to its crossing instant rather than snapped to the
  communication grid.
keywords:
  - co-simulation
  - hybrid systems
  - heterogeneous simulation
  - runtime model switching
  - FMI
  - OpenSim
  - finite-element method
  - structural dynamics
